                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Innovative and relatively unique chain scoring horizontal shooter very dependent on shot timing and not button mashing.   Your shot's strength, let's call a shot a triggering munition, is based on a power bar at the bottom of the screen which in turn means the game requires patience while under pressure to build the power required to initiate a comprehensive screen clearing chain reaction.\n\nUnexploded ordinance piles up behind you further limiting your secure and protective area.  Touch a boundary you die, touch any part of the pile you die, touch anything unexploded  you die.  With additional stages the game becomes progressively challenging with each stage ending in an enhanced battle requiring a proper chain reaction to declare victory.\n\nThe game was developed using XNA which means according to the developer that a full screen option could not be included.  Further, the game will start windowed partially off-screen.  No matter, solved easily with utilities like Lossless Scaling here on Steam that will allow you to play full screen and in 4K or 4K scaled (set your desktop to 4K) which is ideally the optimal resolution, that is 3840x800 .  Lossless Scaling's demo also serves this purpose so no additional purchase required.  \n\nThe game looks fantastic in 4K and significantly adds to the overall experience.  The game is tagged with partial controller support though I was able to execute every functional aspect with a controller.  Easily a Steam hidden gem.  Awesome concept, challenging, achievements etc...  A++.",
